input.findings:
## Summary

Two source edits are needed (3 lines + 8 lines). The feature is implemented by translating `matrix.x/y.length: n` into an internal `n`-element array of `null`s and feeding it to the existing `_initByDimModelData()` path — the existing "null value" handling already auto-generates unique cell values (`X0..Xn-1` / `Y0..Yn-1`), so no other machinery changes. I verified this matches the upstream Apache ECharts implementation (commit `5e54f9db17`, "feat(matrix): Support matrix.x/y.length for conveniently create a headless matrix without composing an array.", files touched: `src/coord/matrix/MatrixDim.ts` +8, `src/coord/matrix/MatrixModel.ts` +3, `test/matrix.html` +44). The local tree is an older snapshot of those files (no license header in MatrixDim.ts, no `coordClamp` in MatrixModel.ts), but both edit sites are byte-identical in context, so the patch applies cleanly.

---

## 1. `src/coord/matrix/MatrixModel.ts` — add the option type

Current code, `src/coord/matrix/MatrixModel.ts:147-155`:

```ts
interface MatrixDimensionOption extends MatrixCellStyleOption, MatrixDimensionLevelOption {
    type?: 'category'; // For internal usage; force be 'category'.
    show?: boolean;
    data?: MatrixDimensionCellLooseOption[];
    // `levels[0]`: the topmost (for x dimension) or leftmost (for y dimension) level.
    // If not specified, use null/undefined, such as `levels: [null, null, {levelSize: 10}]`
    levels?: (MatrixDimensionLevelOption | NullUndefined)[];
    dividerLineStyle?: LineStyleOption;
}
```

Insert three lines after `data?:` (line 150). Exact replacement for lines 147-155:

```ts
interface MatrixDimensionOption extends MatrixCellStyleOption, MatrixDimensionLevelOption {
    type?: 'category'; // For internal usage; force be 'category'.
    show?: boolean;
    data?: MatrixDimensionCellLooseOption[];
    // A simple way to provide column/row count if no need to compose a `data`.
    // Note: `length` is ignored if `data` is specified.
    length?: number;
    // `levels[0]`: the topmost (for x dimension) or leftmost (for y dimension) level.
    // If not specified, use null/undefined, such as `levels: [null, null, {levelSize: 10}]`
    levels?: (MatrixDimensionLevelOption | NullUndefined)[];
    dividerLineStyle?: LineStyleOption;
}
```

Notes:
- `MatrixDimensionOption` is a non-exported interface used only at `MatrixModel.ts:38-39` (`x?`/`y?` on `MatrixOption`), `:182`, `:232` (`defaultDimOption`), `:326` (`class MatrixDimensionModel extends Model<MatrixDimensionOption>`). Nothing else in the repo references it (`rg MatrixDimensionOption` → only that file), so no other type declaration needs syncing.
- Do NOT add `length` to `defaultDimOption` (`MatrixModel.ts:232-241`); absence must remain distinguishable from a value so the series-data-collect path still works.

## 2. `src/coord/matrix/MatrixDim.ts` — consume it in the constructor

Current code, `src/coord/matrix/MatrixDim.ts:125-145` (constructor; the data-parse branch is at 132-144):

```ts
    constructor(dim: 'x' | 'y', dimModel: MatrixDimensionModel) {
        this.dim = dim;
        this.dimIdx = dim === 'x' ? 0 : 1;
        this._model = dimModel;

        this._uniqueValueGen = createUniqueValueGenerator(dim);

        let dimModelData = dimModel.get('data', true);
        if (dimModelData != null && !isArray(dimModelData)) {
            if (__DEV__) {
                error(`Illegal echarts option - matrix.${this.dim}.data must be an array if specified.`);
            }
            dimModelData = [];
        }
        if (dimModelData) {
            this._initByDimModelData(dimModelData);
        }
        else {
            this._initBySeriesData();
        }
    }
```

Exact replacement for lines 132-144 (two hunks: one added line, one added `else if` block):

```ts
        let dimModelData = dimModel.get('data', true);
        const length = dimModel.get('length', true);
        if (dimModelData != null && !isArray(dimModelData)) {
            if (__DEV__) {
                error(`Illegal echarts option - matrix.${this.dim}.data must be an array if specified.`);
            }
            dimModelData = [];
        }
        if (dimModelData) {
            this._initByDimModelData(dimModelData);
        }
        else if (length != null) {
            dimModelData = Array(length);
            for (let i = 0; i < length; i++) {
                dimModelData[i] = null;
            }
            this._initByDimModelData(dimModelData);
        }
        else {
            this._initBySeriesData();
        }
```

Type-safety check (done): `Model.get` is overloaded as `get<R extends keyof Opt>(path: R, ignoreParent?: boolean): Opt[R]` (`src/model/Model.ts:94-96`), so `dimModel.get('length', true)` is typed `number` once step 1 lands. `dimModelData` is `MatrixDimensionCellLooseOption[]`; `Array(length)` is `any[]`, assignable. `tsconfig.json` does not enable `strictNullChecks` (only `strictBindCallApply`), so assigning `null` elements compiles — same as the pre-existing `cellOption = {value: null}` at `MatrixDim.ts:180`/`:185`.

## 3. Why no further changes are needed (mechanism)

`_initByDimModelData` (`MatrixDim.ts:147-272`) already fully supports `null` entries — the code comment at `MatrixDim.ts:435` states "Additionally, `matrix.x/y.data: [null, null, ...]` is allowed":

- `traverseInitCells` (`:170-188`): a `null` option hits the final `else` → `cellOption = {value: null}` and `invalidOption` stays `false` (guarded by `if (option != null)`), so no dev error is logged.
- One cell per locator, each with `span = (1,1)`, one level created (`_levels[0]`, `:216-222`), `_leavesCount = n` (`:154`).
- `postInitCells` (`:237-271`) pops locator 0..n-1 in order, so `ordinal === firstLeafLocator === index` for every cell; then `self._uniqueValueGen.ensureValueUnique(categories, _cells)` (`:253`) replaces each `null` category via `makeUniqueValue()` (`:428-430`) with `X0, X1, ...` / `Y0, Y1, ...` and rewrites `cell.option = defaults({value}, cell.option)` (`:446`). So the auto cells are addressable both by locator/ordinal index and by the generated names.
- `_ordinalMeta` is built with `needCollect: false, deduplication: false` (`:255-259`), leaves get `type = leaf` and `span[otherDim] = _levels.length - level = 1` (`:262-267`), then `_initCellsId()` + `_initLevelIdOptions()`.

Everything downstream (`Matrix._resize` → `layOutUnitsOnDimension`/`layOutDimCellsRestInfoByUnit` in `src/coord/matrix/Matrix.ts:325-421`, `getLocatorCount`, `getUnitLayoutInfo`, `MatrixView.renderDimensionCells` at `src/component/matrix/MatrixView.ts:137-177`, `parseCoordRangeOption` in `matrixCoordHelper.ts`) reads only `_cells`/`_levels`/`_leavesCount`, so it works unmodified. `MatrixModel.optionUpdated()` (`MatrixModel.ts:290-310`) passes the whole merged `x`/`y` option object into `MatrixDimensionModel`, so `length` reaches `dimModel.get('length', true)` with no plumbing change.

